{
  "requirement": "Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted edits to the book that the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only clause is: \"Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted edits to the book that the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.\" It sets no structural obligation. It names no library, algorithm, signature, type, field, or delegation through a named interface. It only says what the skill's instructions must tell agents to do, and when.\n\nSuppose the instruction sat in a different section of `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, such as `section[Workflow]`, or were worded differently. It would still satisfy the text as long as it tells agents to ask before drafting. So the placement and wording are discretionary.\n\nThe supplied root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is where the instruction would appear. The outline reads showed only elided text under `section[Habeas%20requirements]/section[Workflow]`, so I could not confirm the instruction is there. That belongs to a behavioral or content review, not a structural one. No implementation reference is needed to meet a structural obligation.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one observable obligation. Before drafting, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to ask the user whether uncommitted book edits the agent did not make in the current task belong to the task.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_asks_about_foreign_edits_before_drafting]` covers it:\n- It uses `step_of` to find the workflow step containing \"If it has uncommitted edits you did not make in this task, ask the user whether they belong to it\". `step_of` panics if no step contains that phrase, so dropping the instruction fails the test.\n- It asserts that the same step contains \"Run `git status` on the book's source directory\", so the instruction stays tied to detecting uncommitted book edits.\n- It asserts that the ask step's number is lower than the number of the \"Write drafts\" step. That enforces \"before drafting\".\n\nIn `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, step 1 holds the check and the ask, and step 2 is \"Draft. Write drafts…\". The skill meets the ordering the test asserts.\n\nThe test would fail if the ask were removed, moved after drafting, or detached from the `git status` check. I found no other obligations or boundary cases, and the test carries a {test} marker.",
